=Grade the following student assignment.

## RUBRIC:
{{ $('Google Docs — Fetch Grading Rubric').first().json.body.content }}

## ASSIGNMENT TITLE:
{{ $('Code — Parse Filename Metadata').first().json.assignment_title }}

## COURSE:
{{ $('Code — Parse Filename Metadata').first().json.course }}

## STUDENT SUBMISSION:
{{ $('Code — Parse Filename Metadata').first().json.assignment_text }}

Return ONLY this JSON structure with no markdown or code fences:
{
  "total_score": <number 0-100>,
  "rubric_breakdown": {
    "coverage": { "score": <0-25>, "comment": "..." },
    "accuracy": { "score": <0-25>, "comment": "..." },
    "depth": { "score": <0-25>, "comment": "..." },
    "originality": { "score": <0-25>, "comment": "..." }
  },
  "grade_letter": "<A/B/C/D/F>",
  "feedback_paragraph_1": "Overall assessment of what the student did well (2-4 sentences).",
  "feedback_paragraph_2": "Specific areas where the submission could be improved with concrete suggestions (3-5 sentences).",
  "feedback_paragraph_3": "Encouragement and actionable next steps for the student (2-3 sentences)."
}

